 "_notes": [
  "The printed issues. Edit by hand, then run npm run export (people, graph, tables) and npm run build (search).",
  "contents: one entry per piece, page = the PDF page where it starts (the printed number matches). authors and illustrators join the people graph; links land on that spread.",
  "Page text and scans come from the PDFs: python3 -I scripts/extract_pdfs.py n1=<pdf> n2=<pdf> n3=<pdf> n4=<pdf>. Add scans + set pages when a PDF is in.",
  "Names use the spelling already in the archive so people merge (Cuducos, Frederick van Amstel, Georgia Graichen Bueno).",
  "N4 p. 36: the table of contents credits Thiago Pestillo Seles, the page credits Henrique Lindner; the page credit is used.",
  "team: the coordinators from the masthead; every credited person of the issue links to them in the graph.",
  "search: false ends the piece before it without becoming a result (tables of contents).",
  "date: when the issue came out, for its pieces in the archive tables (the day is a convention: the 1st of the month it launched). Without it they show the year.",
  "N3 has no PDF: its scans are photos flattened by python3 scripts/extract_photos.py n3 <photos dir> (corners in scripts/n3-photos.json). The spread printed as pp. 70–71 wasn't photographed, so from the Referências on, pages run two behind the printed numbers (Referências is p. 70 here, 72 in print). Credits from the index and the pages: the photographer and the models of Soluções Razoáveis go under illustrators; pp. 52 and 66 are ads; revisão (Marina Werneck, Patrícia Talhari) stays off, like the other issues' masthead beyond the coordinators. Bruna Carmona Bonifácio is Bruna Bonifacio and Luís Gustavo Padilha Costenaro is Luís Gustavo P. Costenaro (archive spellings); Ivan Alexander Mizanzuk, Julio Teodoro Costa, Marcus Vinícius Pilleggi and Victor Hugo Kebbe use theirs.",
  "N1: pages 2, 3 and 32 are ads. Portfolio pieces are titled by their project; Érik Gurski Lima is Eryk Gurski (N2), Julio Teodoro Costa is Julio Teodoro (N3)."
